# PART 3 — INTELLIGENT LEGAL DOCUMENT IDENTIFICATION

## 5. Legal document type detection

Every uploaded document must first be assigned a document type.

The AI must recognise the difference between a court judgment, an interim order, a final order, a tribunal decision, a petition, a written statement, a rejoinder, an affidavit, a legal notice, a contract, an agreement, a statutory provision, a Bare Act, an amendment, a government notification, a regulation, a circular, a research paper, a legal article, an opinion, a court filing, an evidence document and a client correspondence record.

It must not classify a document simply by its filename. A file called `judgment.pdf` might contain an order, a case note or an unrelated document. A document containing the name of a court is not necessarily a judgment.

Inspect the document's headings, opening paragraphs, case title, court identity, case number, date, parties, signature block, operative directions, statutory references and document structure.

If the AI cannot establish the document type with sufficient confidence, it must assign a provisional type and place the record in a document-verification queue.

The document type should be separate from the legal subject category. A judgment about property disputes is still a judgment; Property Law is its subject area. A research paper about arbitration is still a research paper; Arbitration is its subject.

